; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Stack of Plates
; CATEGORY: Lists & Data Structures
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     stack, push, pop, lists, animation
; SUMMARY:  Plates are pushed onto a stack and popped off again, and the turtle draws the pile after every move.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A stack works like a pile of plates in a kitchen: you can only
;   put a new plate on the top, and you can only take the top plate
;   off. The program pushes five colored plates, then pops three,
;   redrawing the pile each time so you can watch it grow and shrink.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch the turtle world. The command center prints
;   each PUSH and POP and what the stack list looks like.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * PUSH adds a thing to the front of a list kept in a variable
;   * POP removes the front thing and outputs it
;   * the front of the list is the "top" of the stack
;   * last in, first out (LIFO)
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Push more plates. What happens when the pile reaches the top?
;   * Try to POP from an empty stack and read the error message.
;   * Change DRAWPLATE so plates are drawn as ellipses.
; ============================================================

; The whole stack lives in one variable. An empty list means no plates.
make "plates []

; Draw one plate as a filled rectangle with its color name on it.
to drawplate :color :y
  penup setxy -90 :y pendown
  setheading 90 setpencolor "black
  filled :color [repeat 2 [fd 180 rt 90 fd 24 rt 90]]
  penup setxy -20 :y - 17
  setpencolor "white
  label :color
end

; Redraw the whole pile. The stack list keeps the top plate FIRST,
; so we reverse it to draw from the bottom of the pile upward.
to drawstack
  clean
  setpencolor "black setpensize 4
  penup setxy -120 -200 pendown setheading 90 fd 240
  setpensize 1
  localmake "y -200
  foreach reverse :plates [
    drawplate ? :y + 24
    make "y :y + 28
  ]
  penup setxy -150 230 setpencolor "black
  label (sentence [Plates on the stack:] count :plates)
end

to addplate :color
  push "plates :color
  print (sentence [push] :color [->] :plates)
  drawstack
  wait 40
end

to takeplate
  ; POP outputs the top plate AND removes it from the variable.
  localmake "top pop "plates
  print (sentence [pop gives] :top [->] :plates)
  drawstack
  wait 40
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setlabelheight 16
drawstack
foreach [red orange forest purple blue] [addplate ?]
repeat 3 [takeplate]
print (sentence [The plate on top now is] first :plates)
